WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(laughs)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:02.300
- "Marcus Makes a Movie", this is a book

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.820
that I decided to write
to inspire the youth.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.120
The generation today, I feel
like the word no is powerful.

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.780
It's discouraging and
sometimes you do need a,

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.680
a little, a little push
and understanding that

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.150
no is not forever.

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.450
It's, it's a moment.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.350
And this is the book of a guy,

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.990
a young kid that heard the word no

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.460
and didn't want to accept it.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.500
And he wanted to create his opportunity,

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.160
which is what life is about.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:29.480
It's about creating and
making opportunities,

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.690
making the best of them

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:33.720
and having the ambition, the
drive to do it, stay with it,

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.110
ultimately succeed.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.080
For whatever that level of success is.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:41.420
In this case, it was about
making his dream movie

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:43.780
that he was told he couldn't
do because he had no money,

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:44.670
he had no cameras.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.820
And he found a way to do it
without having those assets,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.090
but by just having the help
of some friends, ambition,

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:53.360
and ultimately a dream.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:55.710
And the dream comes true,
but it's a nice journey.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:56.543
It's a good journey.

00:00:56.543 --> 00:00:58.340
And I want kids to understand,
that's what life is.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.173
(clapping)

00:00:59.173 --> 00:01:02.680
Life is a journey, a journey
worth living and embracing.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:03.520
You know why?

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.530
Because at the end of it,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.390
we all get to look back at our story.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.460
And Marcus's story, it's amazing.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:09.800
Wow, did I sum that up.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:10.726
Hit me with it.

00:01:10.726 --> 00:01:11.559
(laughing)

00:01:11.559 --> 00:01:12.761
(drums beating)

00:01:12.761 --> 00:01:13.594
Yes.

00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:14.894
(laughing)

00:01:14.894 --> 00:01:16.738
- That was awesome. I feel inspired.

00:01:16.738 --> 00:01:17.571
- I'm crushing this.

00:01:17.571 --> 00:01:18.404
- First of all right now...

00:01:18.404 --> 00:01:19.237
- I'm crushing.

00:01:19.237 --> 00:01:20.960
- What, what was your experience like?

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.320
I don't know, did you ever have,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.169
were you ever told no about
something and then you feel like

00:01:24.169 --> 00:01:26.360
you pushed through anyway,
that you could do it.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:28.150
Somebody told you you can't
do something and you did?

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:29.560
- Well Kelly, first and foremost

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.730
let me take the time to
echo what you just said.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:32.730
- Okay.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:34.421
- Because Kelly that was a
great, it was a great question.

00:01:34.421 --> 00:01:35.254
Right?

00:01:35.254 --> 00:01:36.087
- Okay, I feel, I feel...

00:01:36.087 --> 00:01:36.920
- I was told, I was told no.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:37.753
- Okay.

00:01:37.753 --> 00:01:40.070
- We all were told noes at
some point in time Kelly.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.850
But here's the thing, my
noes ultimately became

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:47.159
my drive and want toward my yes. Right?

00:01:47.159 --> 00:01:47.992
- Okay.

00:01:47.992 --> 00:01:48.910
- I was told that I wasn't funny.

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:50.930
I was told that I wasn't going to make it.

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.280
- What jackass told you that?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.113
- Several.

00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:56.930
I was told that my movies
would never show overseas,

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.830
and do business overseas.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.987
I was told the likelihood
of me being a movie star,

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:02.490
was not likely.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:04.050
I was told everything.

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:04.883
- Wow.

00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:06.630
- That is the complete
opposite of what I now am.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.390
And here's the thing,

00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:12.290
when I was told that I didn't
get angry, I didn't get mad.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:14.850
I just used it as
personal fire for myself.

00:02:14.850 --> 00:02:15.813
- Yeah.

00:02:15.813 --> 00:02:17.040
- Because I believed in a certain thing

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:18.320
that I felt I had.

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:19.153
- You are Marcus.

00:02:19.153 --> 00:02:20.047
- I am Marcus.

00:02:20.047 --> 00:02:20.880
- Yeah.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.280
- Marcus comes from me.
It comes from my life.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.630
And my story, we just did it in a way

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:28.360
to where kids would be able
to identify with it as well.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.193
- Yeah.

00:02:29.193 --> 00:02:31.320
- But the word no, once
again, it's temporary.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.450
It's not forever, man.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:33.410
And that's the biggest thing that

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:35.620
I want this young generation
to truly understand.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:36.870
- I love that, dream big.

